* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-vco-decap-momcap (issue #23, Part of #16)
* AC sweep of a single-pole R_src-C_decap network: an ideal series source
* resistance R_src (representing a plausible, NOT measured, on-chip/PDN
* source impedance feeding vco.VDD_VCO -- no post-layout parasitic
* extraction exists yet, see RECORD-001 "What this does not bound") driving
* XCDECAP (cap_cmomi, w=70u l=70u) plus a parallel MOM-uncertainty delta cap.
* Reports the resulting -3dB corner frequency directly from a real ngspice
* AC sweep, rather than only the closed-form 1/(2*pi*R*C) -- this exercises
* the same compact cap_cmomi model the real VCO decap instance uses, not an
* idealized linear capacitor alone.
*
* Template placeholders: @RSRC@ (source resistance, ohms), @DELTA_F@ (a
* linear delta capacitor in Farads added in parallel, representing
* +/-MOM_FRAC * C_nominal -- see
* ../../sg13cmos5l-loop-filter-momcap/testbench/tb_extract_c.sp.tmpl for the
* rationale), @TEMP@ (degC), @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@ (resolved filesystem path --
* ngspice's `.include` parser does not expand shell/OS environment
* variables, issue #43).

.include @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cap_cmomi.lib
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@

Vsrc vdd 0 dc 0 ac 1
Rsrc vdd vdd_vco @RSRC@
Xcdecap vdd_vco 0 cap_cmomi w=70u l=70u mmin=1 mmax=4 feed=double subblock=0 m=1 mm_ok=1
Cdelta vdd_vco 0 @DELTA_F@

.control
ac dec 20 1 1000meg
let magdb = db(vm(vdd_vco))
print magdb
.endc
.end
